# Hartree-Fock on Li+ in water: the polarizable continuum model against a
# closed-form answer.
#
# A point charge q inside a spherical cavity of radius R in a dielectric eps
# has the Born polarization energy -(1 - 1/eps) q^2 / (2R). PCMSolver builds
# the cavity for a single atom as one sphere of radius 1.2 x 1.82 A (Bondi
# radius of Li, scaled), i.e. R = 4.1272 bohr, and PCMSolver's water has
# eps = 78.39, so the Born value is -0.119603 Eh. Li+ is a 1s^2 core with
# no charge outside the sphere, and the PCM energy this deck prints
# (the `PCM` line, 1/2 <sigma|V>) is -0.119563 Eh: 0.03 % above Born, the
# discretization of the sphere into ~200 tesserae at area 0.3 A^2.
#
# The k=6 rung reproduces that number to all printed digits, so a single rung
# is enough. Needs a build configured with -DENABLE_PCM=ON.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc scf_li_pcm_born.in)

dft
    xc        hf
    pcm_data  water
    protocol  [1.e-4]
    maxiter   10
    econv     1e-4
    dconv     1e-3
    charge    1
end

pcm
    solver_type  iefpcm
    area         0.3       # average area of a tessera [Angstrom^2]
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
